Chapter: Pr87Deck
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 PR 87 falsifier 2, the first of the two untried corners: a self tail
 call at non-full arity wrapped in `deck-record`, which is typed
 `a -> a` and so does not change the expression's type.

 RENAMED 2026-08-26 22:2x: this probe was called `fd`, and our own
 prelude has a local named `fd` (finding 54), so zig refused on the
 shadow before reaching anything this probe is about. The compiler
 verdict was clean and stands; the zig half was masked and is what the
 rename recovers.

 PREDICTION: CDX2001, for the same reason their arm E refused --
 wrapping the self-application in anything at all stops it being a bare
 self-application in tail position, and the type is unchanged, so the
 body still has a function type where Integer is wanted.

Section: Functions

  deck-self : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  deck-self (x) (y) = deck-record (deck-self x)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (deck-self 1 2))
  end
